35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that big digging is risky because of clay and slippage. Also, we can only hoard the southern part easily.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"Oh dear. It turns out planted areas are three times more expensive to maintain than paved ones, and our staff is tiny.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems our water works last well, but our trees and paving do not. We must be careful with planting.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"Our internal staff is very low, but we have volunteers for habitat work and sports. We rely on contractors for turf.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"People use the park as a shortcut to the tram, avoiding the edges. Also, the drainage is failing and it's getting too hot.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, if people stay on firm ground, maybe we shouldn't do too many soft paths?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly! And if the budget is tight, a forest or wetland sounds like a financial nightmare.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shizue,,But the water basin from years ago is still perfect. Perhaps a water-based plan is the most durable?,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"We have volunteers for habitat and sports, but not for general gardening. That limits our options.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,The heat is an issue. A paved plaza would just be an oven. We need something that manages water and heat.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"If we do something in the south, we can keep the park open. Big earth-moving is the problem.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,I can't support anything that triples our annual spend. A plaza is the cheapest to keep.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"A plaza is just more paving to patch, like the civic hall. I prefer the lasting nature of the basin.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"If we choose sports, we have the volunteers. If we choose habitat, we have volunteers.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,A plaza ignores the drainage crisis and the heat. We need a solution that actually works with the land.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,I'm worried about the clay. A big plaza or sports courts might need too much digging.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,Let's be realistic about the money. We can't afford a high-maintenance garden.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shizue,,Let us look for the path of least resistance and longest life.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,We must balance the available manpower with the environmental needs.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"We need a plan that handles the water, provides shade, and doesn't block the tram commuters.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
