60,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option C is in the south, which is easier to build. But Option D might be too much digging in clay.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,Option B is the only one that won't bankrupt us in three years. Planted areas are too expensive.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shizue,,Option A is risky because our trees often die. Option D is like the basin that lasted eight years.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,We have volunteers for both D and C. But D helps with the drainage issues Shunichi mentioned.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option B is a heat trap. Option A blocks the main gate. Option D solves the drainage and heat.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@May, would a wetland be too expensive? It's mostly water and reeds.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,The ledger says water-managed ground is triple the cost of hard surfaces. It's a budget killer.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shizue,,But it lasts! I would rather pay a bit more for something that doesn't fall apart.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"We have a dedicated habitat volunteer group. That reduces the ""bought-in"" cost for Option D.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Option D is the only rational choice. It addresses the drainage, the heat, and the land's behavior.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I'm leaning towards D if the digging is shallow, but C is safer for the schedule.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,I still say B. It's the only one that's fiscally responsible for the city's long-term accounts.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I cannot vote for more paving. I vote for the wetland. It is peaceful and durable.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree with Shizue. The volunteer support for habitat work makes Option D viable.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,Option B is a failure of imagination and engineering. Option D is the only one that fits the site.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'll go with D. It seems to be what the land and the people need most.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,"I'll be the one complaining about the budget in three years, but I'm outnumbered.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shizue,,It is a lovely choice for the community.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,It is the most sustainable choice given our staffing.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Finally, a decision based on reality rather than a brochure.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
